#### Alternate approach (from GROK... incomplete???)
### # Vivado generated / temporary / cache directories (safe to delete/recreate)
### .Xil/
### *.cache/
### *.runs/
### *.sim/
### *.ip_user_files/
### *.gen/               # Especially .gen/sources_* and DCPs inside
### *.hw/                # Hardware Manager debug sessions
### 
### # Logs, journals, backups, crash files
### *.jou
### *.log
### *.str
### vivado*.debug
### vivado_pid*.str
### *~
### *.backup*
### *.old
### .DS_Store            # macOS junk, if you ever edit on Mac
### 
### # Bitstream and large binaries (re-generated on build)
### *.bit
### *.bin
### *.mcs
### *.elf                # If you ever add soft-core later
### 
### # Simulation / waveform junk
### *.wdb
### *.wcfg
### xsim.dir/
### *.vcd
### *.vpd
### *.fsdb
### 
### # IP output products that regenerate (keep .xci/.xcix for MIG config!)
### *.dcp                # Checkpoints - huge and regenerate
### *.edn
### *.ngc
### *.ngd
### *.edf
### *.sdf
### *.stub.v             # Auto-generated stubs if any
### 
### # Project-specific ignores (add if you see other cruft)
### *.lpr                # Sometimes in .hw/
### *.ltx                # Debug probes
### 
### # Optional: If you regenerate everything via scripts/Tcl and don't commit .xpr
### # proj150.xpr        # Uncomment only if using pure scripted flow
### 
### # Keep your sources explicitly (these are already added via git add, but helps clarity)
### !proj150.srcs/
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/imports/
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/imports/src/
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/imports/src/*.v     # Your Verilog files
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/imports/src/*.vh    # If any headers
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/ip/                 # MIG .xci / .xcix lives here usually
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/ip/**/*.xci*
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/constrs/            # If you have .xdc here
### !proj150.srcs/sources_1/constrs/*.xdc

